Why Is Demand Increasing
Sustainable Chemical Production — BPED technology can generate acids and bases from salts through an electrically driven membrane process, reducing reliance on conventional chemical separation routes.
Lithium Supply Chain Expansion — Growing lithium extraction and brine-processing activity is opening new applications for bipolar electrodialysis systems.
Water Recycling & Recovery — Increasing water-reuse requirements are creating opportunities for BPED in closed-loop processing, salt recovery, and resource-efficiency applications.

Industry & Sustainability Watch: Membrane Separation Gains Momentum
Bipolar electrodialysis is moving from specialized applications toward broader industrial deployment as manufacturers seek lower-energy separation technologies and improved resource efficiency. The technology is being evaluated across chemical manufacturing, wastewater treatment, food processing, pharmaceutical production, desalination, lithium extraction, and recycling. Advanced membranes, modular systems, hybrid configurations, and process-control technologies are supporting wider commercialization.

